  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Climate Information Integrity through the support of the Brazilian co-presidency in the GIIICC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNESCO, the Government of Brazil and the UN launched the Global Initiative on Information Integrity for Climate Change (GIIICC) to help policymakers, media, educators and the private sector uphold high standards of climate-related information and, in turn, rebuild public trust in science-based climate action. 
This project is focused on supporting the Brazilian government efforts as co-president of the Global Initiative, underwriting activities under each GIIICC pillar. By supporting the establishment of governance bodies and its ongoing activities, showcasing results at COP 30 in Bel&#xe9;m, and amplifying those lessons through regional and global fora, the project ensures that GIIICC is well-functiong and also projected internationally as a model for safeguarding information integrity on climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
